 "Yes, I'm prescribing an antiviral medicine.": "./audio/cards/776e219fe045490e70c1.mp3",
 "Please start it today.": "./audio/cards/29c96ff6f348f364ac8d.mp3",
 "But even if he misses a dose, the flu usually gets better on its own in four or five days.": "./audio/cards/46c363ed3395f619ef72.mp3",
 "So there's no need to worry about that.": "./audio/cards/bffaddc63d2166be4a80.mp3",
 "For the fever, please use only acetaminophen.": "./audio/cards/40ffee43ff49c9d4e079.mp3",
 "If you have other kinds of fever medicine at home, please don't use them this time.": "./audio/cards/a3c583a05e34ecfe8dc8.mp3",
 "Yes, one important thing.": "./audio/cards/9a9d544885e507bf3ce9.mp3",
 "For the first two days of the fever, please don't leave him alone.": "./audio/cards/4fcf85e62975257dfdf7.mp3",
 "Some children suddenly run off, or try to go out of a window.": "./audio/cards/8ae6e391ce2da28cd981.mp3",
 "This can happen whether or not they're taking the medicine.": "./audio/cards/67342dc3bc285b8365d1.mp3",
 "So please lock the windows and the front door, and keep him where you can see him.": "./audio/cards/418bfcc6d7b80fb276de.mp3",
 "He needs to stay home until five days have passed since the fever started, and also two days after the fever has gone.": "./audio/cards/a46b6856809296da5494.mp3",
 "If the fever lasts longer, we count again from the day it goes down.": "./audio/cards/d253a138c1c2b08e8b09.mp3",
 "Please come back if the fever lasts three days or more, or if he starts coughing hard or wheezing.": "./audio/cards/960a0e6ad36a8cf55948.mp3",
 "If he has trouble breathing, looks pale, or is too drowsy to respond, please go to the emergency room, even at night.": "./audio/cards/99a989e53bb4b3ce0835.mp3",
 "Otherwise, if he's getting better, you don't need to come back.": "./audio/cards/57b882d655cc2aac8495.mp3",
 "For the first two days, please stay close to him.": "./audio/cards/0f9bcba70c3559f87c55.mp3",
 "Children with the flu sometimes act strangely all of a sudden, like running outside.": "./audio/cards/4d454b3467092c2abd85.mp3",
 "So it's safer to keep the doors and windows locked.": "./audio/cards/e65455c178d145a85d7c.mp3",
 "Her throat is quite red, and the test came back positive for strep.": "./audio/cards/d05a802d6e5456b9d777.mp3",
 "So this is strep throat, not just a cold.": "./audio/cards/2e6eb3924e16191361f4.mp3",
 "It's a common infection in children, and antibiotics work well for it.": "./audio/cards/0354501596e3b845bf1d.mp3",
 "I'm prescribing an antibiotic for ten days.": "./audio/cards/154b83ecad06a97fb39d.mp3",
 "She'll probably feel better in two or three days, but please finish all ten days.": "./audio/cards/4535eb0d798a6852cf98.mp3",
 "The rest of the course helps prevent rare problems with the heart and the kidneys.": "./audio/cards/2f94a0f2b969c9a85ab7.mp3",
 "It does spread easily in the family.": "./audio/cards/00299b513c52289fa5e0.mp3",
 "If he gets a sore throat or a fever, please bring him in and we'll test him too.": "./audio/cards/19e22a2e0020a63d6c62.mp3",
 "Yes.": "./audio/cards/be0f833e51605607da4d.mp3",
 "If the fever or the sore throat doesn't improve after two or three days of the medicine, please come back.": "./audio/cards/288f4e1efcb9bf7586f5.mp3",
 "Also, in the next few weeks, if her urine looks reddish-brown, or her eyelids or legs look puffy, please bring her in.": "./audio/cards/5c7d831300b042afec46.mp3",
 "No, please keep going for the full ten days, even if she feels fine.": "./audio/cards/c3fdaa8d3b61ba6667a9.mp3",
 "That's the important part.": "./audio/cards/ee5936c0f007b7c2f8cf.mp3",
 "I've checked his throat, ears and chest, and this looks like a common cold.": "./audio/cards/e9804b0ac9d73495b844.mp3",
